>> Sure enough:
>>
>> bavlamdei
>> d1=b1=l1 is tomorrow; d1=b1=l1 is the day following b2=l2, day standard
>> d3.
>>
>> Now I'm wondering, what would I use to fill in the third place? i.e. how
>> would I say "We are presenting tomorrow, by day standard (days this class
>> occurs)"?
>>
>> Actually, now I'm wondering how to say "We are presenting tomorrow."  My
>> abstractions and tenses aren't that good yet.
>>
>> PS
>> We in this case is {mi'a}: I and others unspecified, but not you, the
>> listener
>>
>   "mi'a jarco ca lo bavlamdei be fi lo ctufau" should do nicely.
